# The 72 panels of one Polyhedra turn, recorded from the Dis version (appl/wm/polyhedra.b
# with its zx/math modules) in a private 640x560 guest: /dev/time bound to
# 1700000006000000, wm/wm wm/polyhedra -p 3, the 400x400 panel at (4,126) captured 250
# times. The tiles in polyhedra_dis.png, 8 per row, are these panels in hash order.
# Limbo and Ziran round the accumulated vertex positions differently in the last bit, so
# four of them draw a face-boundary pixel one step away; the check allows four pixels.
